ruan: UniXNU-sheng's zzzzzzzzzzz-sheng-edge-matrix.patch for xnu-12377 (same scheduler, same zzyf-sheng-amp.patch), A55 for
sheng's A510 in the comments. Needed for armcpu-edge=1 (ArmCpu calls ml_cpu_init_completed once every core started): the zzyf
matrix closes P->E for FIXPRI/FG/IN but opens it for DF/UT/BG, which sched_edge_config_verify_non_decreasing_qos_strictness
rejects (assert -> panic on DEVELOPMENT; ruan-smp-sigp.patch turns that into a log line), and its E->P steal-only edge never
opens the steal search (scr_incoming_migration_allowed needs FIXPRI migration). Here P->E is closed for every bucket and E->P
steals with weighted-spill weight; FIXPRI may migrate E->P to open the steal search. Counters (index 0 E, 1 P):
sheng_edge_cross_type_steals, sheng_edge_idle_beside_excess, sheng_edge_idle_beside_queued[2][8].
Without armcpu-edge=1 nothing here runs except the counters in the steal path (all edges stay closed).

